# Normalise line endings so a checkout is the same on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files whose SHA-256 is recorded as provenance are exempt from any conversion at all.
# Git rewriting a line ending would silently invalidate a hash that other documents cite,
# which is the one failure this repository cannot tolerate quietly.
data/catalog/*.json      -text
tools/bakeoff/corpus.jsonl   -text
tools/bakeoff/queries.jsonl  -text

# Recorded query vectors. Binary, and read back as the exact bytes that were written: a line
# ending rewritten inside a float array is a silently different vector, which retrieves a
# different control and misses every answer recorded against it. `-diff` because there is nothing
# in it a person can read, and a textual diff of three thousand bytes of floats buries the
# recordings that are meant to be reviewed.
data/fixtures/queries/vectors.npy  -text -diff

# The baked corpus snapshot, a gzip of the ingested vectors and their provenance. Binary for the
# same reason the query vectors are: a rewritten byte is a corrupt restore. `-diff` because a gzip
# stream is not something a person reads in a review.
data/corpus/corpus.sql.gz  -text -diff
